    "id": "i1",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     14,
     26
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies the preserveEscapes toggle on StrSubstitutor. The template \"${not-escaped} $${escaped}\" contains two variable-like tokens: - \"${not-escaped}\" — a normal variable reference that should be replaced. - \"$${escaped}\" — an escaped sequence (escape char '$' followed by \"${escaped}\"). When preserveEscapes is false (the default), the escape character is consumed and the literal text \"${escaped}\" is emitted, giving: \"value ${escaped}\". When preserveEscapes is true, the escape character is kept in the output so the result retains the original \"$${escaped}\", giving: \"value $${escaped}\"."
   },
   {
